From be20433691bcda3262484b174e937f43e0853f01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:16:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] [jakompiled] wasm backend: 128-bit vf/integer
 instructions, &var, 128-bit args and returns

- vf math (add/sub/mul/div/min/max/xor/sqrt), blend, splat, swizzle, itof/ftoi as wasm SIMD,
  with the exact AVX results (vminps/vmaxps operand order, vcvttps2dq out of range)
- 128-bit integer ops (pext*, pcpy*, pceq*, pcgt*, logic, psubw, packuswb, paddb, shifts,
  byte shifts, pshuflw/hw)
- variables whose address is taken live in the function's frame on the GOAL stack
- 128-bit arguments / return values through a fixed SIMD argument area
- vnop / vwaitq are no-ops; behavior self doesn't count toward the 8 argument limit
---
